        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.318,
            0.882,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": "3. In a quadrilateral ABCD, suppose AB ‖DC and $\\mathrm { A B } \\neq \\mathrm { C D } .$ . Suppose G and H are the midpoints of AC and BD respectively. Prove that GH $\\parallel \\mathrm { A B }$ . (Why did we assume $\\mathrm { A B } \\neq \\mathrm { C D ? ) }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.373,
            0.387,
            0.613,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.45,
                0.502,
                0.548,
                0.521
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 12.24"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.535,
            0.881,
            0.574
          ],
          "content": "4. Suppose the midpoints of sides AB, BC, CD and DA of a quadrilateral ABCD are P, Q, R and S respectively."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.574,
            0.658,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "(i) Show that PR and QS bisect each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.593,
            0.88,
            0.632
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Show that if $AC = BD$ then PR and QS are perpendicular. Is the converse true?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.642,
            0.769,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": "5. Suppose PQRS is the Varignon parallelogram of ABCD."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.674,
            0.79,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.451,
                0.792,
                0.549,
                0.812
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 12.25"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.82,
            0.883,
            0.919
          ],
          "content": "(i) Copy only PQRS on another paper. Show how you will recreate a congruent copy AʹBʹCʹDʹ of ABCD from PQRS. This will be relevant when we return to study tilings at the end of this chapter. (**Hint:** How will you place vertex Aʹ? How will you place Bʹ, Cʹ and Dʹ?)"
        }
